### Main

The *Main* section brings the general pages of the site:
- **Home**: presents the project and its goals (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('67d7c3ae-93f6-4d31-82b3-21bbb33218fe'); return false;">Home</a></i>);
- **Acknowledgement**: honors people and institutions that contributed to the project (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('be49a7ce-25c1-4a4d-9063-ce662c6d059d'); return false;">Acknowledgement</a></i>);
- **Partners and Collaborators**: lists the site's partners and collaborators (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('22c43176-5923-4e70-b7f9-fece7d0cfdc3'); return false;">Partners and Collaborators</a></i>);
- **Contact**: informs how to reach the team (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('498a1507-8742-45fa-bf4c-390c0a2ef50b'); return false;">Contact</a></i>);
- **Licence**: explains the licences of the software and the content (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('d03d759b-a5f7-4273-bb69-7b92addf81b1'); return false;">Licence</a></i>);
- **Version**: presents the site's version history (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('3800034f-54d5-4107-8174-7845a1a112a8'); return false;">Version</a></i>);
- **Gallery**: lists the images used by the project, organized by source (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('7be43264-1905-4ed4-a94a-478acc722134'); return false;">Gallery</a></i>);
- **Documentation**: teaches how to navigate and use the site (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('4bbb0ce6-5e99-4291-a156-d3e343da8743'); return false;">Documentation</a></i>).

### Sciences

The *Sciences* section gathers the texts that introduce scientific thought:
- **The Knowledge**: presents the different types of intelligence and the construction of knowledge (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('81e9393b-d5b6-4b04-91bd-417e943d3e97'); return false;">The Knowledge</a></i>);
- **Scientific Method**: introduces the scientific method and its importance (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('44acb900-ee84-4e42-8d9b-a947351af2cd'); return false;">Scientific Method</a></i>);
- **Sources**: shows the sources used in the site's research (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('0d449896-8388-4a24-8885-11e20a687d88'); return false;">Sources</a></i>);
- **Philosophy**: presents different philosophical views linked to science (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('0fbf1a0d-4e41-4b0a-ae82-bcdb7bbc6693'); return false;">Philosophy</a></i>).

### Other science sections

The remaining menu sections bring specific studies:
- **First Steps** (*The Foundations*): introduces the first mathematical concepts (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('c4fa2c15-7df0-4754-971a-dae503516d51'); return false;">First Steps</a></i>);
- **Universe** (*The Foundations*): studies Physics and the universe (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('258c7689-f89b-411b-ac87-476920ddb085'); return false;">Universe</a></i>);
- **The Origin of Matter** (*Chemical*): studies the origin of matter (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('99ecb0ef-d04f-423e-9121-5986c0dac12d'); return false;">The Origin of Matter</a></i>);
- **Atlas** (*Geography*): gathers historical maps (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('f140d8d6-80cc-4d82-b9f7-c3ba06bf2ed3'); return false;">Atlas</a></i>);
- **The Origin of Life** (*Biology*): studies the origin of life (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('09e6d6a5-0db6-496e-9dab-53b51348a52b'); return false;">The Origin of Life</a></i>);
- **Understanding Texts** (*Literature*): explores the comprehension of texts (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('2806b294-0d2a-4ca2-8008-b2b82791427a'); return false;">Understanding Texts</a></i>).

### History, Genealogy, and Indigenous

*History* brings:
- **General History**: studies cultures and civilizations (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('4ec952d8-0422-4688-9d69-5787cfa8cdf5'); return false;">General History</a></i>);
- **Genealogical Trees**: presents the history of families (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('8abed0b5-2e6f-49b4-85bf-c62aad3bbcd1'); return false;">Genealogical Trees</a></i>);
- **Myths and Believes**: discusses myths and beliefs about our ancestors (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('b733064c-ae29-4480-b42c-c73b94238ef9'); return false;">Myths and Believes</a></i>);
- **Historical Events**: presents different versions of remarkable events (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('61a5aa2b-c9ff-4e0c-9b86-dcdfa4c3fcba'); return false;">Historical Events</a></i>).

*Genealogy* brings:
- **F.Q.A.**: answers common questions about genealogy (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('8dac70eb-9efc-41bd-bd86-52e3c1423f46'); return false;">F.Q.A.</a></i>);
- **My Ancestors**: guides the first steps in genealogical research (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('e21391d8-f158-454f-a677-531f9e8d23a0'); return false;">My Ancestors</a></i>).

*Indigenous* brings:
- **Chronology**: presents the chronology of indigenous peoples (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('c5492aa1-67c3-4794-95f3-c7ff05bac191'); return false;">Chronology</a></i>);
- **Who ... ?**: proposes questions to reflect on concepts (<i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('b85db11c-8ef2-446c-aaaf-6888090be9a5'); return false;">Who ... ?</a></i>).
